  "_approach": "Kick-dropout build: bar 1 is a heavy 4/4 garage bump; bar 2 removes the kick entirely and lets a shaker bed plus accelerating clap stutters (8ths then 16ths) and a low-mid-high tom climb carry the tension. The loudest clap+snare lands on the last 8th and the final 16th is left empty for the drop. Ref: the kick-drop-then-return trick documented for UKG build-ups; Shanks & Bigfoot 'Sweet Like Chocolate' breakdown exit.",
